Redis is a in memory key value data strucutre, it has nothing to do with postgres,sql, mongodb, and works seprately
redis can be used a queue using list but we do not use that because
1.Job loss->what if worker failed after poping a job
2.no retry system 
3.Parrallel workers->When you have multiple parallel workers reading from a Redis List, they are competing blindly. There is no server-side coordination.

Redis Lists don't have a concept of Consumer Groups. Without consumer groups, you miss out on native features like:

Load balancing tasks evenly across workers automatically.

Tracking exactly which worker has been assigned which specific task.
 
Inspecting how long a task has been pending or stuck with a slow worker.

